### Seam walk — drive the activity-construction bridge over HTTP.
###
### Run the host:  dotnet run --project src/Apps/Elsa.Server/Elsa.Server.csproj
### Use with the REST Client (VS Code / Visual Studio / Rider).
###
### On boot, the CLR reconciliation source scans the host output folder and catalogs the two CLR
### activities (WriteLine + WorkflowDefinitionActivity, DescriptorType = ClrActivityDescriptor). Steps 1–2
### below add a *workflow-as-activity* row (DescriptorType = WorkflowIdentity). Step 3 lists the mix;
### step 4 crosses the construction seam for any row.
###
### NOTE: CShells path-routing mounts the default shell under "/default" (see appsettings
### CShells:Shells:default). All routes below are therefore under {{host}}/default/...

@host = http://localhost:5095/default

### 1. Create a workflow definition (Workflows.Design). Note the returned `id` + `version`.
###    (A real workflow would carry a WriteLine node; construct-only doesn't require it yet.)
POST {{host}}/design/workflows/definitions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Greeting workflow",
  "description": "A workflow we will expose as an activity."
}

### 2. Catalog that workflow AS an activity (Activities.Design) — descriptor type = WorkflowIdentity.
###    Paste the DefinitionId / VersionId / Version from step 1's response into DescriptorPayload.
###    (Construct-only: placeholder identity values are fine — they just round-trip through the constructor.)
###    KNOWN ISSUE: this currently returns HTTP 400 (a pre-existing IObjectMapper failure mapping the
###    response DetailsView) but the row IS persisted — confirm with step 3's list. Tracked separately.
POST {{host}}/design/activities/definitions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "activityTypeKey": "Acme.Workflows.GreetingWorkflow",
  "sourceKind": "Workflow",
  "sourceId": "greeting-workflow",
  "descriptorType": "Elsa.Workflows.Primitives.Models.WorkflowIdentity",
  "descriptorPayload": {
    "DefinitionId": "<paste DefinitionId>",
    "VersionId": "<paste VersionId>",
    "Version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "category": "Composed",
  "displayName": "Greeting workflow (as activity)"
}

### 3. List what the publishing surface can construct — see the descriptor-type mix:
###    the WorkflowIdentity row from step 2 + the two CLR (ClrActivityDescriptor) rows from reconciliation.
GET {{host}}/publishing/activities

### 4. Inspect the compiled contract surface for one row. Paste an ActivityVersionId from step 3.
###    CLR rows expose canonical type aliases and stable plain-property inputs. WorkflowIdentity rows remain
###    discovery metadata until the typed child-workflow execution boundary is implemented.
GET {{host}}/publishing/activities/<paste ActivityVersionId>/construct
